<title>USA: High Plains Wheat -Basis flat, sales seen moderate.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat -Basis flat, sales seen moderate.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bids for hard red winter wheat were steady on Monday but movement was expected to be moderate in anticipation of a higher KCBT opening, several High Plains grain dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The phone has been ringing all morning but most of these guys are going to wait until they see how the board opens,&quot; a Kansas merchandiser said. &quot;I think they'll sell a higher open.&quot;</p>
<p>Wheat futures were called to open a shade higher, following expected gains in corn and soybeans which were seen opening sharply higher on generally dry U.S. Midwest weather.</p>
<p>&quot;I think once we open we might buy some wheat with the calls a little higher,&quot; an Oklahoma merchant said.  </p>
